# Page patterns

Build new pages from the existing pieces. Do not invent a second carousel, card, or heading.

- Routes stay thin. Compose in `view/`, sections in `components/reususables/`, copy in `lib/content`. The `reususables` folder name is intentional.
- The page column and the navbar share `max-w-council` (`83rem`, 1328px), with `px-5 md:px-10 min-[1408px]:px-0`. Do not give either a different cap.
- The about page uses `PageIntro` (“Our Story” / “About Ikorodu” / “North LCDA”), then the introduction with the headquarters photograph, the impact figures (they count up when the row scrolls into view), the three history chapters, the five-ward section from the homepage, the green community band, and the “Know your council” links. Each ward card opens its community page. The history uses the council’s published record: created in 2003 from Ikorodu Local Government, five wards (Isiu, Odogunyan, Olorunda, Erikorodo, Agbala), headquarters at Isiu, and the chairmen named on the council about page. Do not restore the bracketed draft lines or the round figures 500K+, 50+, 20+ and 15+. Hidden layers stay off: the archive verification note and the “Help tell the story” band.
- A ward page follows the Isiu frame: a green introduction with the ward name on the left and a rounded photograph on the right, the five-ward switcher, the overview beside local facilities, projects, and local news. Isiu has no concern band. The other four wards include “Have a concern”. Project and news buttons open `/projects` and `/news`.
- The executive council page uses `PageIntro` (“Leadership” / “Executive Council”), then the chairman’s office: a green portrait card beside a brief written from his published record (eight years as Vice Chairman, Executive Chairman from July 2025, the New Deal, and the first hundred days). Email and phone stay as drawn. Under that, “Meet your council.” is a three-column portrait grid, and every portrait is shown, including Hon. Abiodun Salau and Hon. Basirat Adewunmi Babatunde. The agriculture supervisor is Hon. Olawale Ogunbela JP. Phone and email stay as drawn, including `+234 801 000 0000` and `chairman@ikorodunorthlcda.gov.ng`. On a phone, each card adds the short biography and hides it from `lg`. The related links are Legislative Members, Management Team and Departments.
- The legislative house page uses `PageIntro` (“Representative Arm” / “Legislative House”), then the civic-mandate band: “Chamber overview” beside the description, and the three duties Representation, Local lawmaking and Public oversight. “Meet your representatives.” is a portrait grid of the five councillors named in that frame. Roles stay in the frame’s wording, including “Councilor” and the ward codes. The pending responsibility line stays on every card. Homepage team cards keep their own names.
- The departments page uses `PageIntro` (“Service Network” / “Departments”), then a searchable directory with the filters All departments, Departments, Units, and Health & environment. Each card shows the icon, title, description, email, and the unfinished phone `+234 XXX XXX XXXX`. View profile appears only when the department has its own page. Hidden layers stay off, including “Headed by…” and the completed badges. “How to reach a department” keeps the three steps and the bracketed phone and email placeholders.
- The management team page uses `PageIntro` (“Administration” / “Management Team”), then the administrative-arm band and a three-column portrait grid. Roles use the full title, including “Head of Department” and the department name. Names, roles and photographs come from the council’s management folder: Mr. Nairu Abayomi Samsideen, Bankole Esther Oluyemi, Awonusi Ademola A, Mr Amori Muritala Kehinde, Mr. Akiode Oluwaseyi O., Mr Ogunleye Akintope Abayomi, Eng. Akinsanya Sunday, Dr. Wajero K T, Com. Olawore Elijah, Mr Ganiyu Abideen Maiyegun, Mr Japhet O Enemunhe, Mr Ahoton Jameson Thona and Barr. Amusa Adebayo Aminat. The education portrait file is named “HOD Education”; the person is Mr Ganiyu Abideen Maiyegun. Related links are Executive Council, Legislative Members and Departments.
- The ICT department page uses `PageIntro` with the label linking back to `/government/departments`. The title breaks after “Information &”. The body is the about copy, eight responsibilities, and a desk card for Mr Amori Muritala Kehinde. The phone stays `+234 XXX XXX XXXX`. Other departments are Finance & Accounts, Education & Library Services, and Primary Health Care, including “HOD: [Head of Department]”.
- Suggest a project is `/projects/suggest`, reached from the projects banner. It uses `PageIntro` (“Community input” / “Suggest a project”), then the four steps, then the suggestion form beside the tips and the “Need help?” card. Keep the bracketed lines, including `[responsible department]`, `[contact method]`, `[timeframe]`, `[planning or budget cycle]`, `[Phone number]`, `[street name]`, `[Accepted formats]`, `[file size limit]`, `[department phone]`, `[department email]` and `[Office hours]`. The category menu lists Roads & drainage, Water, Health, Education, Environment, Markets, Youth & sports and Other. The ward menu lists the five wards. The designer note “Project category dropdown shown open for reference.” stays off the page. Sending the form opens the visitor’s email to `info@ikorodunorth.gov.ng`.
- Landmarks & culture is `/landmarks`. It uses `PageIntro` (“Places & heritage” / “Landmarks & culture”), then a filterable list of published places, then Eweye Day and the traditional leadership. A photograph sits beside the copy when one exists for that place. Places stay inside Ikorodu North: the Marriage Registry at the Isiu secretariat, LASUSTECH and First Gate, the Odogunyan industrial estate, 174 Battalion, the Eweye palace, Isiu Market, the farm settlements, and the Ikorodu–Shagamu corridor. Do not add the wider Ikorodu heritage trail. Caleb University’s campus is in Imota LCDA, at Km 15, Ikorodu–Itoikin Road, so it stays off this page. The new Eweye palace foundation was laid in April 2025; do not describe that palace as finished.
- The contact page uses `PageIntro`, then the message desk: contact cards on the left and the enquiry form on the right. Under that, the visit block pairs the secretariat photograph with the address and office hours. Hidden layers stay off: the emergency advisory, the directions card, and the helpful-contact guidance. Sending the form opens the visitor’s email to `info@ikorodunorth.gov.ng`.
- The projects page uses the news listing pieces: `PageIntro`, `NewsToolbar`, `FeaturedNewsCard`, `NewsCard`, and `SectionHeading`. A project story uses `ArticleLayout`, the same frame as a news article. The story body spans the full council column. Under the body, `PhotoGallery` shows the project photographs side by side. Clicking a photograph opens it in a popup. Homepage project rows still use `HomeStoryCard`. List only verified commissioned works: Odo-Nla health centre, the WaterAid handovers, Adamo–Araro Road, the Apeka–Agbala culverts, High School Road and Army Children School, the Igbaga classrooms, Omigo and Maya. News uses the same published record, including the first 100 days, Iranlowo Owo Apa and the July 2025 swearing-in. Do not restore the bracketed draft stories. New posts stay on the council Facebook page: `https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61578369553900`.
- Story rows use `HomeCarousel` with `bleed` and `autoSlide`, inside the same `max-w-council` column as the heading. Section is `overflow-x-clip`. Left edge matches the content column by measuring the column, never `100vw`.
- Cards share `HomeStoryCard`: equal size, title and description `line-clamp-2`. Story titles are `text-xl font-semibold`. Department titles are semibold and one step larger than the original card title. Projects show date and category pills. Announcements end with `Read more`. Arrows sit on the right. Add real news items when there are not enough cards to slide.
- Section titles use `HomeSectionHeading` with `titleClassName="font-bold"`. On small screens the title is `text-[26px]`; it steps up from `md`. A heading link uses the section `cta` (projects → `/projects`, announcements → `/news`).
- Wide intro copy spans the title column. Pass `descriptionClassName="max-w-none"` when the paragraph must match the heading width, as on departments. The wards heading spans the full heading row (`columnClassName="max-w-none flex-1"`). Its description is two lines, split after “verified projects,”. The wards themselves are a selector beside one large photograph: choosing a ward changes the photograph. The photograph keeps the short bottom gradient, the cream label, a white name, landmarks at 72% white, and a gold Explore link.
- The team heading breaks as “Ikorodu Local” / “Government Team”, and its type is one step larger than the default section title. Its description is two lines, split after “professionals”.
- Keep unfinished Figma wording exactly, including `[community]` and names such as “Hon jimoh Idris iliasu” / “Chip Whip”. Replace a placeholder only when the user supplies the finished line.
- The homepage map section background stays cream through most of the block, then fades to light green (`#e0eba7`) at the bottom. The map itself is a real OpenStreetMap of Ikorodu North. Pins and the feature list use located facilities: the Isiu secretariat and marriage registry, 174 Battalion, the Lagos Ministry of Health centres that can be placed, public schools named in council and local reports, Isiu Market, and Lucky Fibres. Do not add Losi Oba PHC, Eruwen Health Post, or Olorunda PHC until a real coordinate exists. Do not restore parks, the drawn map, “ON THE MAP”, `[Council secretariat address]`, or the old placeholder counts. Clicking a feature filters the pins. “View Full Map” stays at the bottom of the feature card.
- The chairman message is the exception. It uses his published record: eight years as Vice Chairman, Executive Chairman from July 2025, and his stated priorities of infrastructure, healthcare, education, sanitation, security, youth and small-business opportunity, and open, accountable government. Do not restore the `[key focus area]` draft.
- Leave hidden Figma layers off the page (utility strip, “How can we help you?”). The shared footer keeps contact details, without office hours, the “YOUR COUNCIL. YOUR COMMUNITY.” eyebrow, “Our Contact Info.”, or the LOCATION label.
